<programme start="20261024043000 +0000" stop="20261024050000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">TrueSouth</title><sub-title lang="en">Upstate SC</sub-title><desc lang="en">Singleton grew up in Greenwood, S.C. and now lives on the outskirts of Spartanburg with his partner Glenda Guion, a ceramicist; they make their living as artists, working in side-by-side backyard sheds, accompanied by their dog, Cleo.</desc><category lang="en">Travel</category><category lang="en">Food</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15917551_b_v11_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261024050000 +0000" stop="20261024053000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">TrueSouth</title><sub-title lang="en">Jasper, Ala.</sub-title><desc lang="en">The crew joins their guide Caleb Johnson at the onetime center of the Alabama coal mining industry as they document the legacies of that hard work; Johnson has plenty of familiarity with the area as grew up in the nearby town of Arley.</desc><category lang="en">Travel</category><category lang="en">Food</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15917551_b_v11_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261024053000 +0000" stop="20261024083000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Duke at Virginia</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Virginia Cavaliers clash with the Duke Blue Devils in ACC conference play. Virginia relies on quarterback Beau Pribula after his rushing touchdown against SMU, while Duke counts on Nate Sheppard following his 98 receiving yards on October 17.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261024083000 +0000" stop="20261024113000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">NC State at Stanford</sub-title><desc lang="en">The NC State Wolfpack face the Stanford Cardinal in an ACC regular-season matchup at Stanford Stadium. Both teams currently sit in the bottom half of the conference standings. Stanford defeated Elon 34-7 behind Micah Ford&apos;s four touchdowns.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
